Actually this is an interesting point. Say the target is polynomial of deg p. You would probably observe a 'convergence' of lr for all width m=d^k for all integer k <p. If you were to tune on small width say at m=d you would select optimal eta for m<d^2/log. But at m=d^2 you would see a jump in the optimal eta.
